{"id":"prescribers-on-lists","title":"Prescribers on a federal or State list, and prescriptions filled afterwards","question":"Is any San Francisco prescriber in the Medicare drug file also on a federal exclusion list, the list of revoked Medicare enrollments or the State suspended list, and were prescriptions under that number filled in a later year?","finding":"17 of the 10,061 provider numbers that appear in the San Francisco drug files for 2018 to 2024 are on one of the lists. For 5 of them the file shows prescriptions filled in a calendar year after the year of listing: the largest is Juan Posada (provider no. 1265496301): Medicare enrollment revoked, 2021-01-27 (424.535(A)(3) Felonies), with 6,865 claims costing $885,453 in 2022.","how":"Provider numbers in the federal Part D files for San Francisco prescribers were matched to the inspector general's exclusion list, the federal list of revoked Medicare enrollments and the State Medi-Cal suspended list. Matches are by provider number only, never by name. \"After\" means claims in a calendar year later than the year of listing, so same-year claims are not counted.","limits":"The files do not say what a revocation, exclusion or suspension does to prescriptions already written, or whether a drug plan may still fill that person's prescriptions; those rules are not on disk. Refills of prescriptions written before the listing would be filled afterwards, and the lists do not say where the conduct took place. The file counts fills, not prescriptions written. Lists without a provider number for the person are missed entirely. The Part D file ends in 2024, so anything listed since cannot show.","tier":"OFFICIAL","columns":[{"k":"who","t":"Name on the list","type":"person"},{"k":"kind","t":"Federal prescriber type","type":"text"},{"k":"list","t":"List","type":"text"},{"k":"listed","t":"Date listed","type":"date"},{"k":"until","t":"Until","type":"text"},{"k":"reason","t":"Reason as listed","type":"text"},{"k":"inFile","t":